Z||000003||fiero56||04-27-2000||11:55 PM||||Just want to double check this. No-one here has a 3.4 v-6 installed in their Fiero? I am interested in the differences in power, possible cam changes, anything else to help get a little more juice out of it, and also, what type of exhaust note it will produce compared to my 2.8.<P>Any takers?||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||04-27-2000||11:59 PM||||YES please. I have this 88GT sittin around that I have been wanting to do something with and here all this about the 3.4 and have even e mailed to Ed a couple of times and got some great info but would really like to hear from the people who have had one awhile. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||04-28-2000||09:27 AM||||I'm interested in the swap, too. As a matter of fact, I'm just about to go and pick up a 3.4 today. I don't have anything to put it in right now but... that's another thread.<P>Doing some number crunching, it seems the be the best swap for the dollar. Those numbers assume that you can drill the starter holes yourself or at least buy one of the jigs from Fieroshop ($125) and do it your self.<P>Logically from 2.8 to 3.4, there is a ~20% increase in cubes, therefore, there shoud be a minimum of a ~20% gain in torque. GM sells a cam and lifter set for around $100 that add power in the 1500-4500 RPM range and says with 3.4 springs under the valves is good to 6000 RPM. And is recommended for compression ratio on 8.9 to 9.5. I don't have any specific numbers but I'd be willing to guess that those numbers translate to over 200 HP.<P>I talked to a guy at the Daytona show last year who just had a stock 3.4 installed and drove it down to the show. He couldn't hardly talk because the smile on his face was so big.<P>Being logical about it, stock Gen II 3800, Gen II 3800 SC, or SBC is going to be faster but, they are also a LOT more $$$$. I'm going to the 3.4 instead of a 2.8-3.1 rebuild.<P>Just ramblin,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000006||87PegasusGT||04-28-2000||01:30 PM||||I already have a 3.4 but the mechanic is still installing it. Torque is 195lbs hp=160||||reg||1
Z||000007||KnightRyder31||04-28-2000||01:50 PM||||My buddy has a 355CI engine in his 86 GT.<BR>Fast as heck, you wouldnt believe it! He says it will do 0-60 in under 5. Thats awsome. He says his 1/4 mile time is under 11. He also has a NOS hook-up.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||04-29-2000||12:27 AM||||My 3.4 project has been on hold for a few weeks, but now may be getting back on track. I will be burning the midnight oil this weekend to see how far I get. I already have the cradle out and 2.8 engine/tranny off the cradle. Now, I will have to spend the time transferring all the bolt-ons to the 3.4- I will keep everyone posted.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierosound||04-30-2000||12:34 PM||||MooCow...  <P>I think the site below has the most complete info on building a 3.4L I've found so far.  It covers some of the swap issues (which can be found elsewhere), but more importantly, it has details on a performance rebuild. It also answered my question on increasing compression without buying exotic $$$ pistons from Keith Black or JE, by using pistons from the 3.4 DOHC.  Go to the homepage to get his viewpoints on the results after the engine was installed.<P> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html</A> ||||reg||1
